"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[85912],{85912:e=>{e.exports='# Databricks Private CLI\n\nUse this skill when executing commands with the `runDatabricksPrivateCli` tool. This tool provides a CLI-style interface backed by internal workspace APIs for asset discovery and notebook management.\n\n## Command Format\n\n- Provide only the command group, action, and arguments — no `databricks` prefix.\n- Commands dispatch to real workspace capabilities; they do **not** shell out to the `databricks` binary.\n- Commands do not require user approval (no guardrail prompt).\n\n## Available Command Groups\n\n- **assets** — Search, discover, and read workspace assets (tables, notebooks, queries, dashboards, pipelines, jobs, files, alerts, endpoints, models, folders)\n- **notebooks** — List, edit, and execute notebook cells\n\n## Asset Discovery Best Practice\n\nWhen exploring the workspace or answering data questions:\n\n1. **Start with `assets for-you`** to get the user\'s personalized recommendations\n2. Use `assets search` to find assets by keyword across multiple types\n3. Use `assets read` to get full details of specific assets\n\n## Argument Conventions\n\n### Positional Arguments\n\nSome commands accept positional arguments before flags:\n\n```\nassets search my_table --types tables --limit 3\nassets read notebook 12345\nassets read job 67890\n```\n\n### Flags\n\nNamed arguments use `--flag value` syntax:\n\n```\nnotebooks edit --id 12345 --operation add --content \'print(1)\'\n```\n\n### JSON Payloads\n\nUse `--json \'{ ... }\'` for complex structured inputs:\n\n```\nnotebooks edit --id 12345 --json \'{"operation": "add", "content": "print(1)", "position": 0}\'\n```\n\n### Help\n\nAppend `--help` to any command to see its usage, options, and examples:\n\n```\nassets search --help\nnotebooks edit --help\nassets --help\n```\n\n## Validation\n\nCommands validate required arguments before execution. If a required argument is missing, the tool returns the usage help text automatically.\n\n## When to Load Sub-Topics\n\n### Assets\n\nLoad [`assets.md`](assets.md) when working with:\n\n- Searching workspace assets by keyword\n- Fetching personalized asset recommendations\n- Reading asset details by type and ID\n\n### Notebooks\n\nLoad [`notebooks.md`](notebooks.md) when working with:\n\n- Listing cells in a notebook\n- Adding, updating, or deleting cells\n- Executing a notebook cell on the attached cluster\n'}}]);
